   - **`/data/work/work/workspace/openvela_workspace/nuttx/boards/risc-v/esp32p4/esp32p4-function-ev-board/src/esp32p4_bringup.c`** (READ): dump code with fields M/C/L/S/Q/N; L field = w7[7] = {WRLK(0x5010ff44), WREN(0xff48), WRUN(0xff4c), TDLK(0xff50), TDUN(0xff54), DROP_CNT(0xff58), DROP_CHAR_INTST(0xff5c)}; C field = {jbk(0xff9c), cbuf(0xffa0), csem(0xffa4), cena(0xffa8), cst(0xffac), cfifo(0xffb4)}; S field = 13 words starting at 0x5010ff00. WRLK/WREN/WRUN = ASCII sentinels 0x57524c4b/0x5752454e/0x5752554e.
   - **`/data/work/work/workspace/esp32/esp32-p4/esp/v6.0.2/esp-idf/components/esp_driver_usb_serial_jtag/src/usb_serial_jtag.c`** (READ, lines 55-142): authoritative ESP-IDF ISR showing the ZLP-on-drain mechanism the NuttX driver lacked.
